  "query_preview": "(Saturday through Tuesday)...\nA subtropical low pressure system will move inland into\nsouthwestern California for late Saturday into Sunday.\nThe trend is for greater rainfall for much of southwestern \nCalifornia from the coast to the mountains. Some lighter showers \ncould develop for Saturday afternoon into Saturday evening. The \ngreatest potential for heavier rainfall is for late Saturday \nnight.\n\nThrough Sunday, the ECMWF AIFS ensemble output only has 15 percent\nof members with less than 1 inch of rainfall for San Diego with\nthe greatest rainfall for the east-west mountain ranges from \nVentura County to southwestern San Bernardino County. For Saturday \nnight through Sunday afternoon, the ECMWF Extreme Forecast index \nhas increased rainfall across San Diego County to between the 80th \nand 90th percentile.\n\nIt will be dry with warming for next week with high temperatures\nfor next Tuesday a few degrees above average for coastal areas\nwith inland areas around 5 degrees below average. High\ntemperatures for next Tuesday for the coast and valleys would be \nmostly in the 70s, for the mountains in the mid 40s to mid 60s,\nand in the lower deserts around 80.",
